WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.870
Film Courage:&nbsp; Chad, we have a quote here
from someone, which is an unlikely&nbsp; quote

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.870
regarding acting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.750
It’s from David Bowie.&nbsp;

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.460
I just read it the other day and I found it
interesting.&nbsp;

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:15.860
The quote said “As You Get Older Questions
Come Down to About Two or Three Things:&nbsp;

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:20.560
How long and what do I do with the time that
I have left?”&nbsp;

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.980
And the reason this quote stuck out to me
is that I’m thinking about it in my own

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:28.640
life and I was wondering for you, do this
bring up anything interesting?&nbsp;

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.300
Just because life changes after the 20’s
and…

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:39.590
Chad Lindberg:&nbsp; Yeah…I mean I just turned
40 and so that question definitely looms.&nbsp;

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.420
It’s like how much longer?&nbsp;

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.940
How am I going to go?&nbsp;

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:47.640
And what more do I have to do here?&nbsp;

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.250
There’s a lot to do.&nbsp;

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:53.370
I feel like 40 is the new 20.&nbsp;

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.370
Maybe?&nbsp;

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.370
I don’t know [laughs]?&nbsp;

00:00:55.370 --> 00:01:01.170
It makes me reflect on all of my time that
I’ve spent in Los Angeles and pursuing an

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:02.740
acting career.&nbsp;

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:09.100
And I look back and I’m like “Thank, God!”
because when you’re young you don’t realize

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.100
what you’re getting into, you know?&nbsp;

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.229
And I kind of had my blinders on and I’m
like Nothing is Going to Get Here [gestures

00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:16.229
in front of his eyes].&nbsp;

00:01:16.229 --> 00:01:17.479
I am going to do it.&nbsp;

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:22.880
And I’m very lucky that it happened because
it doesn’t happen for a lot of people.&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.319
So 22 years in, I’m like [exhales a sigh
of relief].&nbsp;

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:27.979
But…it’s still just as hard as it was.

00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:28.979
Film Courage:&nbsp; O.k.&nbsp;

00:01:28.979 --> 00:01:34.789
Well, first off you are an incredibly young
40, so you have this on your side.

00:01:34.789 --> 00:01:35.789
Chad Lindberg:&nbsp; Thank you!

00:01:35.789 --> 00:01:40.891
Film Courage:&nbsp; But now do you think maybe
there will be new roles, maybe not Jesse [in

00:01:40.891 --> 00:01:42.329
FAST AND FURIOUS] or maybe Jesse reinvented?

00:01:42.329 --> 00:01:49.590
There is a whole new thing open to you as
a 40-year-old male where you could still pass

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:50.680
for way younger but…

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:52.451
Chad Lindberg:&nbsp; Yeah…well I appreciate
that.&nbsp;

00:01:52.451 --> 00:01:54.729
I can’t do high school anymore [laughs].&nbsp;

00:01:54.729 --> 00:01:58.571
I’m pushing college age but it definitely
worked for me when I was younger.&nbsp;

00:01:58.571 --> 00:02:03.200
I played…you know, I was age 20 playing
a 15 year old.&nbsp;

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:12.319
So now I can still play thirties but it definitely
lends me to do more interesting roles I think

00:02:12.319 --> 00:02:19.760
because I have grown into myself, I know who
I am, I’m much more confident in who I am.&nbsp;

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:24.230
You know, when you are in the late twenties
to early thirties, I kind of squandered a

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:29.450
bit because I’m like, “Well I don’t
really fit here and I don’t really fit here.”&nbsp;

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:34.239
So now that I’ve come into my forties I
feel very confident about where I am going.

00:02:34.239 --> 00:02:36.980
Film Courage:&nbsp; Where did you think that you
didn’t fit in?&nbsp;

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:37.980
That’s interesting.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:41.460
Because I don’t see you that way….I could
see you fitting into so many roles.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:48.540
Chad Lindberg:&nbsp; Well, I wasn’t quite a
man [laughs] as funny as that sounds.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:54.890
&nbsp; I’m in my early thirties were a really
tough time in this business because I started

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:58.120
out by getting big roles in this business
right away.&nbsp;

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:05.829
I mean I started working off my first audition
I booked and my career started out kind of

00:03:05.829 --> 00:03:06.829
like here.&nbsp;

00:03:06.829 --> 00:03:13.720
And as I was age thirty I kind of had to backtrack
a little bit and sort out what a lot of actors

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:17.360
go through in the beginning of their careers.&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:23.940
Trying to get the hustle and so had to step
back a little bit and reassess everything.&nbsp;

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:32.620
So I wasn’t quite an older guy to play this
role and I wasn’t quite young enough.&nbsp;

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:35.870
Interesting enough in my early thirties it
was an awkward stage for me as weird as that

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:36.870
is.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:37.569
Question for the viewers: What are your thoughts
on how age impacts an actor’s career?

